-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. Coupled neural co-processing basins
-- Two bounded nervous systems (or brain S1 + co-processor S2) coupled by a bilateral channel c
-- (e.g. eye-contact photon coupling or receptive interface) induce a canonical quotient map merging
-- previously separate local basins into a joint co-processing basin (cognitive light cone expansion).
coproc-basin-map : {S1 S2 : Type 0}
                 → (eq1 : S1 → S1 → Bool) → (eq2 : S2 → S2 → Bool)
                 → (s1 : S1 → S1 → Bool) → (s2 : S2 → S2 → Bool)
                 → (c : (S1 × S2) → (S1 × S2) → Bool)
                 → Basins (S1 × S2) (prod-step eq1 eq2 s1 s2)
                 → Basins (S1 × S2) (coupled-step eq1 eq2 s1 s2 c)
coproc-basin-map = basin-prod-coupled
